  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Crowley Government Services has $460M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 255 awards with an average award size of $1.8M. Obligations fell 9.9% year over year. Fiscal-year trends show obligations of $426M in FY21, $429M in FY22, $705M in FY23, $728M in FY24, and $511M in FY25 before the current-year total of $460M. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $347M in obligations, followed by the Department of Transportation with $110M. Deep Sea Freight Transportation is the largest NAICS market at $254M, followed by Freight Transportation Arrangement at $116M and Ship Building and Repairing at $54.5M. Other notable markets include Other Warehousing and Storage at $30.8M, Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $3M, and Petroleum Refineries at $2.3M. The Department of Health and Human Services accounts for $3M and the Department of Homeland Security accounts for $2.4K in FY2026 to date. Figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations except where noted otherwise on award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 9.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals peaked in FY24 at $728M and then declined to $511M in FY25 and $460M in FY26 to date. The Department of Defense, with $347M, drives most of the dollar movement. Large shifts in Deep Sea Freight Transportation at $254M and Freight Transportation Arrangement at $116M also affect the total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are obligations by agency and market?",
        "body": "Obligations are concentrated with a few buyers and NAICS markets. The Department of Defense accounts for $347M and the Department of Transportation accounts for $110M of the $460M total. Deep Sea Freight Transportation at $254M and Freight Transportation Arrangement at $116M are the two largest markets. Smaller markets include Ship Building and Repairing at $54.5M, Other Warehousing and Storage at $30.8M, and Petroleum Refineries at $2.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
